Agreed that this should move to shared inference configuration code. One timing concern: the way I understand this, InferenceMode is [activated by the engine](https://github.com/NVIDIA/Megatron-LM/blob/753297e386cb6d2767c82875dfa635fb463ceb00/megatron/core/inference/engines/dynamic_engine.py#L589), after model/config construction, so checking it only in TransformerConfig init could miss this path.

We could apply the conversion during shared checkpoint-argument preparation, using an explicit inference indicator and the saved QB settings, before router construction and weight loading. This would enable the saved expert bias and disable training balancing across inference entry points.
@Mellonta, does that match the intended global-batch QB inference behavior? Would you prefer this refactor in this PR, or a separate checkpoint-routing PR?

